+---
+id: dl-001-resolvepointer-strictness-own-properties-only-errors-for-unresolved
+type: decision-log
+title: "resolvePointer strictness: own properties only, errors for unresolved"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Other features will build on `resolvePointer`, so its edge-case behaviour must be exact and safe.
+RFC 6901 leaves some outcomes to the evaluating application.
+
+## Decision
+
+- An empty pointer returns the whole document; any other pointer must start with `/`.
+- `~` must be followed by `0` or `1`; otherwise the pointer is invalid and an error is thrown.
+- Array tokens must match `0|[1-9][0-9]*` and be within bounds. The `-` token (past the end) does
+  not refer to a value, so it throws.
+- Object tokens resolve only to own properties (so `/__proto__`, `/constructor` throw), and
+  characters of strings or members of primitives and `null` are never resolved.
+- Every failure throws a plain `Error`.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Safe against prototype-chain access; a later write-oriented feature (e.g. JSON Patch) that needs `-`
+must handle it outside `resolvePointer`. Callers cannot tell invalid from unresolvable pointers by type.
